---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy | Credits That Count"
  description="What Credits That Count collects, what it never collects, how family information is used, and how to have your data deleted."
>
  <div class="container">
    <section class="block" style="margin-top:26px;">
      <h2>Privacy at Credits That Count</h2>
      <p class="muted">Last updated: November 19, 2026</p>
      <p>
        Credits That Count prepares transfer guidance for Louisiana students
        and their families. This page says exactly what information we
        collect, what we never collect, how the information is used, and how
        to have it deleted.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          When a family requests a plan or joins a list: a parent or guardian
          name and email address, the student's current college, the target
          college, and the courses taken or planned, including any AP scores
          the family chooses to share.
        </li>
        <li>
          When a counselor joins the counselor list: a name, organization,
          email address, and the approximate number of students served.
        </li>
        <li>
          Basic visit counts on our pages, recorded without a name attached,
          so we know which tools families use.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>What we never collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We do not ask for transcripts.</li>
        <li>We do not ask for Social Security numbers.</li>
        <li>We do not ask for student account usernames or passwords.</li>
        <li>
          We do not collect or store payment card details. Payments are
          handled by Stripe, and your card information goes to Stripe, not
          to us.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>How the information is used</h2>
      <p>
        Family information is used only to prepare and deliver the product
        requested, to answer questions about it, and, for Plan Monitoring
        subscribers, to keep the plan current. Counselor list information is
        used only to write back about counselor seats.
      </p>
      <p>
        Family information is never sold. It is not shared for marketing. The
        only services that process it are the ones needed to run this site
        and deliver its products, such as our hosting, email, and payment
        providers.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>Students and consent</h2>
      <p>
        Credits That Count is designed for parents, guardians, counselors,
        and adult students. When a request includes a student's course
        information, the person submitting it confirms they are the student,
        the student's parent or guardian, or a counselor working with the
        family, and that they may share that course information with us for
        the purpose of preparing the plan.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Plan records are kept while they are needed to deliver the product
        and, for monitoring subscribers, while the subscription is active.
        Signup and counselor list emails are kept until you ask us to remove
        them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <div class="secgroup">
        <p class="secband">Deleting your data</p>
        <p>
          You can have your information deleted at any time. Write to
          <a href="mailto:plans@creditsthatcount.com?subject=Delete%20my%20data">plans@creditsthatcount.com</a>
          from the email address you used, with the subject "Delete my
          data." We will delete your records and confirm by email within 30
          days.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>Changes to this page</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the updated version will be posted on this
        page with a new date at the top.
      </p>
      <p>
        Questions about privacy can be sent to
        <a href="mailto:plans@creditsthatcount.com">plans@creditsthatcount.com</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="tagline-foot">Know before you go.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
